-- title:
--   A-sections of the X₁(Mp) model land in the smooth locus
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for the set $\{p\}$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ which equals [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map $\mathbb{Q}((q)) \to L((q))$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an algebra structure over which $L$ is its fraction field, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A \to L$, equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be an element, nonzero as a `Fact` hypothesis, whose image in $L((q))$ is the image under the coefficientwise map of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $= q^{-1}\cdot(\text{the rational }j\text{-numerator power series})$. Write $f \colon \mathrm{TwoChartModel}\,A\,K\,j \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ for [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252), the structure morphism of the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $A$-subalgebras of $K$ attached to $j$ and $j^{-1}$. Let $U$ be an open subscheme of $\mathrm{TwoChartModel}\,A\,K\,j$ such that the composite of the inclusion of $U$ with $f$ is smooth of relative dimension $1$, and such that every open $W$ with this property satisfies $W \le U$. Let $\varepsilon$ be a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} A \to \mathrm{TwoChartModel}\,A\,K\,j$ together with a proof that its composite with $f$ is the identity of $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Then the set-theoretic range of the underlying map of topological spaces of $\varepsilon$ is contained in $U$.
--
--   This is the statement that an $A$-valued section of the regular two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over the discrete valuation ring $A$ avoids the non-smooth points of the model, so that sections factor through the maximal relative-dimension-one smooth open; it is the form in which sections are fed into the relative Picard and Néron model constructions for this curve. It is used in the construction of the relative sub-Picard representation attached to the zero cut and in the separation statement for base-changed sections.
